{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement","title":"lem:orthogonal-complement","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2459,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:orthogonal-complement","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:orthogonal-complement","line":4045,"source":"\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lem:orthogonal-complement}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.59}\nIf $(V,q)$ is a finite-dimensional scalar product space and $S\\subseteq V$ is a\nsubspace, then\n\\[\n\\dim S+\\dim S^\\perp=\\dim V.\n\\]\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch The map\n$\\Phi\\colon V\\to S^*$, $\\Phi(v)=\\widetilde q(v)|_S$, has kernel $S^\\perp$.\nEvery element of $S^*$ extends to $V^*$ and $\\widetilde q$ is onto, so $\\Phi$ is\nsurjective. Rank--nullity yields the formula.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section> <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6f7274686f676f6e616c2d636f6d706c656d656e74\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.59</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(V,q)$\">$(V,q)$</span> is a finite-dimensional scalar product space and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S\\subseteq V$\">$S\\subseteq V$</span> is a subspace, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\dim S+\\dim S^\\perp =\\dim V.  \\]\">\\[  \\dim S+\\dim S^\\perp =\\dim V.  \\]</span>  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch The map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi \\colon V\\to S^*$\">$\\Phi \\colon V\\to S^*$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi (v)=\\widetilde q(v)|_S$\">$\\Phi (v)=\\widetilde q(v)|_S$</span>, has kernel <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S^\\perp $\">$S^\\perp $</span>. Every element of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S^*$\">$S^*$</span> extends to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V^*$\">$V^*$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\widetilde q$\">$\\widetilde q$</span> is onto, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Phi $\">$\\Phi $</span> is surjective. Rank–nullity yields the formula. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:polarization-scalar-product","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement-involution","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement-involution","title":"lem:orthogonal-complement-involution","label":"lem:orthogonal-complement-involution"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nondegenerate-subspace","title":"lem:nondegenerate-subspace","label":"lem:nondegenerate-subspace"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:completion-nondegenerate-bases","title":"lem:completion-nondegenerate-bases","label":"lem:completion-nondegenerate-bases"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hyperplane-nondegenerate","title":"lem:hyperplane-nondegenerate","label":"lem:hyperplane-nondegenerate"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthonormal-tail-spans-orthogon